{"id":"malchiah","name":"Malchiah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:malchiah"],"groups":["2. Also called MELCHIAH"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Malchiah","text":"Jehovah’s king. (1.) The head of the fifth division of the priests in the time of David (1 Chr. 24:9). (2.) A priest, the father of Pashur (1 Chr. 9:12; Jer. 38:1). (3.) One of the priests appointed as musicians to celebrate the completion of the walls of Jerusalem (Neh. 12:42). (4.) A priest who stood by Ezra when he “read in the book of the law of God” (Neh. 8:4). (5.) Neh. 3:11. (6.) Neh. 3:31. (7.) Neh. 3:14."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H4441","lemma":"מַלְכִּיָּה","xlit":"Malkîyâh","gloss":"Malkijah, the name of ten Israelites","kjv":"Malchiah, Malchijah","count":13,"share":1},{"strong":"H6583","lemma":"פַּשְׁחוּר","xlit":"Pashchûwr","gloss":"Pashchur, the name of four Israelites","kjv":"Pashur","count":5,"share":0.38},{"strong":"H4641","lemma":"מַעֲשֵׂיָה","xlit":"Maʻăsêyâh","gloss":"Maasejah, the name of sixteen Israelites","kjv":"Maaseiah","count":3,"share":0.23},{"strong":"H4326","lemma":"מִיָּמִן","xlit":"Mîyâmin","gloss":"Mijamin, the name of three Israelites","kjv":"Miamin, Mijamin","count":2,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H5718","lemma":"עֲדָיָה","xlit":"ʻĂdâyâh","gloss":"Adajah, the name of eight Israelites","kjv":"Adaiah","count":2,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H3395","lemma":"יְרֹחָם","xlit":"Yᵉrôchâm","gloss":"Jerocham, the name of seven or eight Israelites","kjv":"Jeroham","count":2,"share":0.15}],"verses":["1Chr.6.40","1Chr.9.12","1Chr.24.9","Ezra.10.25","Ezra.10.31","Neh.3.14","Neh.3.31","Neh.8.4","Neh.10.3","Neh.11.12","Neh.12.42","Jer.21.1","Jer.38.1"],"related":[{"id":"pashur","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.227,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"maaseiah","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.086,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"eleazar-eleazer","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.058,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both